1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,636
Ava: Okay so PyTorch just dropped 2. 14. Almost three thousand commits since 2. 13.
Ava：好吧，PyTorch 刚发布了 2.14。自 2.13 以来，提交次数接近三千次。

2
00:00:07,636 --> 00:00:10,238
That's a lot to unpack.
这么多内容，得好好捋一捋。

3
00:00:10,238 --> 00:00:15,456
Brian: Yeah, 2,995 commits, 487 contributors. It's a big one.
Brian：没错，2,995 次提交，487 位贡献者。这次更新规模不小。

4
00:00:15,456 --> 00:00:21,604
But there's a clear thread running through it if you squint.
不过仔细看，会发现其中有一条清晰的主线。

5
00:00:21,604 --> 00:00:23,154
Ava: Which is?
Ava：是什么？

6
00:00:23,154 --> 00:00:31,044
Brian: PyTorch trying to be one platform that works the same whether you're on NVIDIA, AMD, Intel, or a Mac.
Brian：PyTorch 正努力成为一个统一的平台，让你无论使用 NVIDIA、AMD、Intel 还是 Mac，都能获得一致的体验。

7
00:00:31,044 --> 00:00:36,825
Faster matmuls, a rewritten networking backend, native math on Apple GPUs.
更快的矩阵乘法、重写的网络通信后端，以及 Apple GPU 上的原生数学运算。

8
00:00:36,825 --> 00:00:39,128
Same story, three fronts.
同一个方向，三条战线。

9
00:00:39,128 --> 00:00:43,990
Ava: Let's start with the matmul thing. NVGEMM. What even is that?
Ava：先说矩阵乘法吧。NVGEMM 到底是什么？

10
00:00:43,990 --> 00:00:52,593
Brian: So, GEMM is just General Matrix Multiply — the operation that eats most of your GPU time in a transformer.
Brian：GEMM 就是通用矩阵乘法——在 Transformer 中，它会消耗 GPU 大部分计算时间。

11
00:00:52,593 --> 00:00:58,380
NVGEMM is a new backend for it inside Inductor, PyTorch's compiler.
NVGEMM 是 PyTorch 编译器 Inductor 里的一个新后端，用来执行这项运算。

12
00:00:58,380 --> 00:01:01,466
Ava: And it's built on CuTeDSL?
Ava：它是基于 CuTeDSL 构建的？

13
00:01:01,466 --> 00:01:03,258
Brian: Right, that landed in 2.
Brian：对，这项技术在 2.13 中首次推出，

14
00:01:03,258 --> 00:01:11,096
13 as a way to generate CUTLASS kernels — CUTLASS is NVIDIA's template library for writing fast GPU math.
可以用来生成 CUTLASS 内核——CUTLASS 是 NVIDIA 编写高速 GPU 数学运算的模板库。

15
00:01:11,096 --> 00:01:14,977
In 2. 13 it could only spit out a standalone kernel.
在 2.13 中，它只能生成独立的内核。

16
00:01:14,977 --> 00:01:23,464
Whatever came after, like a bias add, stayed in a separate kernel that had to re-read the result from memory.
后续操作，比如加偏置，都得放在单独的内核里，还要从内存重新读取结果。

17
00:01:23,464 --> 00:01:25,878
Ava: That sounds wasteful.
Ava：听起来挺浪费的。

18
00:01:25,878 --> 00:01:30,250
Brian: It is. So the big addition in 2. 14 is epilogue fusion.
Brian：确实。所以 2.14 的一大新增功能就是尾处理融合。

19
00:01:30,250 --> 00:01:37,484
Now the bias add, the activation, the rescale — they get folded right into the same kernel.
现在，加偏置、激活、重新缩放等操作都能直接融合进同一个内核。

20
00:01:37,484 --> 00:01:39,980
No extra memory round trip.
不必再额外往返访问内存。

21
00:01:39,980 --> 00:01:44,194
Ava: And this competes against what PyTorch already had?
Ava：它是要和 PyTorch 现有的方案竞争吗？

22
00:01:44,194 --> 00:01:47,830
Brian: Exactly, it's not a replacement, it's a third candidate.
Brian：没错，它不是替代方案，而是第三个候选项。

23
00:01:47,830 --> 00:01:54,192
Inductor autotunes NVGEMM alongside Triton and ATen and picks whichever is fastest for your shape.
Inductor 会将 NVGEMM 与 Triton、ATen 一起进行自动调优，针对你的张量形状选出最快的方案。

24
00:01:54,192 --> 00:02:06,552
It also reaches the low-precision paths now, so things like NVFP4 — a four-bit floating format — get their scaling folded into the kernel too, instead of paying for a separate multiply.
它现在也支持低精度计算路径，所以像 NVFP4 这种四位浮点格式，也能把缩放操作融合进内核，不用再单独做一次乘法。

25
00:02:06,552 --> 00:02:08,198
Ava: Any catch?
Ava：有什么限制吗？

26
00:02:08,198 --> 00:02:12,306
Brian: You have to opt in, add NVGEMM to the autotune backend list.
Brian：你得主动启用它，把 NVGEMM 加到自动调优的后端列表里。

27
00:02:12,306 --> 00:02:15,250
And NVFP4 support needs Blackwell hardware.
而且 NVFP4 支持需要 Blackwell 硬件。

28
00:02:15,250 --> 00:02:22,516
If an epilogue is too weird for it to express, it just falls back to Triton, so you're not worse off.
如果某种尾处理操作太特殊，无法表达，它就会回退到 Triton，所以性能不会更差。

29
00:02:22,516 --> 00:02:29,058
Ava: Okay, let's move to distributed training. This is the part I actually care about.
Ava：好，我们来聊分布式训练。这才是我真正关心的部分。

30
00:02:29,058 --> 00:02:30,257
Brian: Big one here too.
Brian：这方面也有重磅更新。

31
00:02:30,257 --> 00:02:41,960
There's a preview of a rewritten NCCL backend — NCCL being NVIDIA's Collective Communications Library, the thing that handles all-reduce and friends across GPUs.
现在提供了一个重写版 NCCL 后端的预览版。NCCL 是 NVIDIA 集合通信库，负责处理 GPU 间的全归约等操作。

32
00:02:41,960 --> 00:02:43,750
Ava: Rewritten how?
Ava：具体怎么重写的？

33
00:02:43,750 --> 00:02:49,256
Brian: It's ported from a project called torchcomms, which showed up in 2. 13.
Brian：它移植自一个名为 torchcomms 的项目，该项目在 2.13 中首次出现。

34
00:02:49,256 --> 00:02:58,949
Now it lands in-tree as basically a drop-in replacement, nicknamed nccl2, and it's slated to become the default backend in 2.
现在它作为基本可直接替换的组件纳入了 PyTorch 源码树，昵称是 nccl2，并计划在 2.15 中成为默认后端。

35
00:02:58,949 --> 00:02:59,532
15.
2.15。

36
00:02:59,532 --> 00:03:02,642
Ava: What does it actually buy you over the old one?
Ava：相比旧版，它具体带来了什么？

37
00:03:02,642 --> 00:03:14,296
Brian: Nonblocking communicators, one-sided memory access, and — this is the headline for me — fault tolerance built in as a first-class concept, not a hack bolted onto NCCL specifically.
Brian：非阻塞通信器、单边内存访问——还有我认为最重要的一点：内置了故障容错，将其视为一等功能，而不是专门针对 NCCL 临时拼凑的补丁。

38
00:03:14,296 --> 00:03:18,601
Ava: Wait, back up. What does fault tolerance mean in this context?
Ava：等等，回头说说。在这里，故障容错具体是什么意思？

39
00:03:18,601 --> 00:03:22,422
Isn't that usually a checkpoint-and-restart thing?
这通常不就是检查点加重启吗？

40
00:03:22,422 --> 00:03:24,280
Brian: That's exactly the pain point.
Brian：这正是最棘手的问题。

41
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:33,980
Normally when one rank dies in a big job, you tear down the whole process group and restart it, which throws away warm state across the entire cluster.
通常，大型作业中只要一个 rank 进程挂掉，就得拆掉整个进程组再重启，整个集群已经预热好的状态也会随之丢失。

42
00:03:33,980 --> 00:03:37,498
Ava: Ouch. That's expensive at scale.
Ava：哎，这种规模下代价可不小。

43
00:03:37,498 --> 00:03:37,893
Brian: Very.
Brian：非常大。

44
00:03:37,893 --> 00:03:48,404
So now the Backend and ProcessGroup objects expose reconfiguration interfaces — a group can be rebuilt in place instead of destroyed.
现在 Backend 和 ProcessGroup 对象都提供了重新配置接口，可以原地重建进程组，而不用销毁它。

45
00:03:48,404 --> 00:03:52,152
And this isn't NCCL-only, Gloo gets it too.
而且这不只适用于 NCCL，Gloo 也支持了。

46
00:03:52,152 --> 00:03:57,302
Ava: You mentioned one-sided memory access. What's that, exactly?
Ava：你提到单边内存访问。那具体是什么？

47
00:03:57,302 --> 00:03:59,666
Brian: Think RMA, remote memory access.
Brian：可以把它理解为 RMA，也就是远程内存访问。

48
00:03:59,666 --> 00:04:04,541
Normally a collective needs both sides to show up and synchronize.
通常，集体通信需要双方都参与并进行同步。

49
00:04:04,541 --> 00:04:13,828
One-sided means one rank can just read or write another rank's memory directly, no matching call needed on the other end.
单边访问则意味着一个 rank 可以直接读写另一个 rank 的内存，不需要对方同时发起匹配的调用。

50
00:04:13,828 --> 00:04:15,810
Ava: When would you want that?
Ava：什么情况下会用到它？

51
00:04:15,810 --> 00:04:17,776
Brian: Irregular access patterns.
Brian：不规则的访问模式。

52
00:04:17,776 --> 00:04:23,826
Embedding lookups, weight transfer, expert routing in mixture-of-experts models.
比如嵌入查找、权重传输，以及混合专家模型中的专家路由。

53
00:04:23,826 --> 00:04:28,184
Anywhere the access pattern isn't a clean all-to-all.
只要访问模式不是规整的全对全通信，都适用。

54
00:04:28,184 --> 00:04:31,294
Ava: And there was something about a Flight Recorder?
Ava：还有个叫 Flight Recorder 的东西？

55
00:04:31,294 --> 00:04:36,996
Brian: Right, that's the trace buffer people use to debug hung or mismatched collectives.
Brian：对，那是用来排查集合通信卡住或不匹配的追踪缓冲区。

56
00:04:36,996 --> 00:04:39,986
It used to be wired specifically into NCCL.
它以前专门接在 NCCL 上。

57
00:04:39,986 --> 00:04:46,522
Now it hooks through ProcessGroup generically, so it works for Gloo or any custom backend too.
现在它通过通用的 ProcessGroup 接入，所以 Gloo 和自定义后端也能用。

58
00:04:46,522 --> 00:04:52,644
Debugging a hang doesn't mean giving up your trace just because you're not on NCCL.
即使用的不是 NCCL，排查卡顿时也能保留追踪记录。

59
00:04:52,644 --> 00:04:58,437
Ava: Makes sense. Let's switch gears — literally, since there's a feature called torch.
Ava：明白。换个话题——还真有个功能叫 torch.

60
00:04:58,437 --> 00:04:59,282
switch.
switch，也就是 torch.switch。

61
00:04:59,282 --> 00:05:00,503
Brian: Ha, yeah. So torch.
Brian：哈哈，对。torch.

62
00:05:00,503 --> 00:05:06,091
cond already existed for a two-way branch inside a compiled graph — if this, else that.
cond，也就是 torch.cond，早就支持在编译图中做二选一分支。

63
00:05:06,091 --> 00:05:13,671
But if you needed, say, eight-way branching, like picking one of eight experts in an MoE model, you had to nest torch.
但如果需要八路分支，比如在 MoE 模型里从八个专家中选一个，就得层层嵌套 torch.

64
00:05:13,671 --> 00:05:14,728
cond calls.
cond 调用。

65
00:05:14,728 --> 00:05:17,238
Ava: Which gets ugly fast.
Ava：那很快就会变得很难看。

66
00:05:17,238 --> 00:05:22,922
Brian: Right, it bloats the traced graph and hides what you're actually doing. torch.
Brian：对，追踪图会膨胀，也看不清实际逻辑。而 torch.switch

67
00:05:22,922 --> 00:05:27,731
switch does multi-way branching natively, dispatching on an index.
可以按索引直接选择多个分支。

68
00:05:27,731 --> 00:05:31,724
It's aimed squarely at mixture-of-experts routing.
它主要就是为混合专家模型的路由设计的。

69
00:05:31,724 --> 00:05:35,986
Ava: There's also something about while loops and CUDA graphs?
Ava：while 循环和 CUDA 图也有新变化？

70
00:05:35,986 --> 00:05:39,983
Brian: torch. while_loop can now be captured inside a CUDA graph.
Brian：现在 torch.while_loop 可以被捕获进 CUDA 图。

71
00:05:39,983 --> 00:05:51,840
Normally a data-dependent loop count forces a device-to-host copy to decide how many iterations to run, and that breaks graph capture right where you'd want it intact.
通常，循环次数如果取决于数据，就得把数据从设备传回主机来决定迭代次数，这会打断图捕获。

72
00:05:51,840 --> 00:05:56,894
Ava: So now the loop count can vary at replay time without breaking capture?
Ava：所以现在重放时循环次数可以变化，也不会破坏图捕获？

73
00:05:56,894 --> 00:05:57,432
Brian: Exactly.
Brian：没错。

74
00:05:57,432 --> 00:06:04,634
The condition gets re-evaluated on GPU at the end of each iteration using CUDA's native while-node support.
借助 CUDA 原生的 while 节点，每次迭代结束时都会在 GPU 上重新判断条件。

75
00:06:04,634 --> 00:06:12,724
It's not a speed win by itself, it just means a variable-length loop no longer kicks you out of the graph entirely.
这本身不会提速，但变长循环终于可以留在图里了。

76
00:06:12,724 --> 00:06:16,658
Ava: Okay, now the one I've been waiting for — Apple Silicon.
Ava：好，终于说到我期待的 Apple Silicon 了。

77
00:06:16,658 --> 00:06:19,818
My Mac finally gets real linear algebra?
我的 Mac 终于能好好做线性代数运算了？

78
00:06:19,818 --> 00:06:22,592
Brian: Yes! This was a genuine gap before.
Brian：是的！以前这确实是个短板。

79
00:06:22,592 --> 00:06:29,250
SVD, eigh — that's the eigendecomposition for Hermitian matrices — QR, and Cholesky.
SVD、eigh——也就是厄米矩阵的特征分解——还有 QR 和 Cholesky。

80
00:06:29,250 --> 00:06:35,624
All were leaning on Apple's MPSGraph framework, or just falling back to CPU.
这些运算以前要么依赖苹果的 MPSGraph 框架，要么回退到 CPU。

81
00:06:35,624 --> 00:06:39,838
Ava: Which kills performance if you're doing anything numerical.
Ava：做数值计算时，这会严重拖慢速度。

82
00:06:39,838 --> 00:06:47,815
Brian: Right, mixed CPU and MPS round trips are exactly the kind of thing that quietly tanks your throughput.
Brian：对，在 CPU 和 MPS 之间来回传数据，会悄悄拉低吞吐量。

83
00:06:47,815 --> 00:06:53,992
Now SVD, eigh, and lstsq run via native Jacobi-style Metal kernels for float32.
现在，float32 的 SVD、eigh 和 lstsq 都由原生的 Jacobi 式 Metal 内核执行。

84
00:06:53,992 --> 00:07:00,405
Cholesky got a faster panel-factorization algorithm too, something like 1. 2 to 2.
Cholesky 也换用了更快的面板分解算法，提速约 1.2 倍到

85
00:07:00,405 --> 00:07:03,492
8x faster depending on matrix size.
2.8 倍，具体取决于矩阵大小。

86
00:07:03,492 --> 00:07:05,234
Ava: Any limits?
Ava：有什么限制吗？

87
00:07:05,234 --> 00:07:11,138
Brian: float64 still falls back to CPU, because Metal simply has no double-precision type.
Brian：float64 仍会回退到 CPU，因为 Metal 没有双精度类型。

88
00:07:11,138 --> 00:07:23,224
And there's a whole separate five-part rewrite of reduction kernels — full reductions, strided ones, argmax and argmin — moving off MPSGraph onto hand-written Metal.
另外，归约内核也分五部分重写了，包括全量归约、跨步归约、argmax 和 argmin，从 MPSGraph 改用手写 Metal 内核。

89
00:07:23,224 --> 00:07:27,918
Ava: I saw something about an 8. 5x slowdown fix too.
Ava：我还看到修复了一个导致速度慢 8.5 倍的问题。

90
00:07:27,918 --> 00:07:32,641
Brian: Yeah, that one's specific but important if you run models locally.
Brian：对，这个问题很具体，但对本地运行模型的人很重要。

91
00:07:32,641 --> 00:07:41,228
Single-token decode — the shape you get when you're generating one token at a time — was falling off the fast path in F.
单 token 解码，也就是每次生成一个 token 时，会错过 F.linear

92
00:07:41,228 --> 00:07:47,732
linear on MPS. Eight point five times slower than it should've been, on bf16 and fp16.
在 MPS 上的快速路径；用 bf16 和 fp16 时，速度比应有水平慢了 8.5 倍。

93
00:07:47,732 --> 00:07:51,874
Ava: That's huge for anyone doing local inference on a Mac.
Ava：对在 Mac 上做本地推理的人来说，这影响太大了。

94
00:07:51,874 --> 00:08:01,248
Brian: Exactly, it's one of the bigger remaining gaps between MPS and CUDA for autoregressive generation, and this closes a good chunk of it.
Brian：没错，这是自回归生成时 MPS 与 CUDA 之间较大的性能差距之一；这次缩小了不少。

95
00:08:01,248 --> 00:08:05,366
Ava: Quick one — what's @dynamic_spec?
Ava：快速问一句，@dynamic_spec 是什么？

96
00:08:05,366 --> 00:08:08,375
Brian: It's a cleanup, not a new capability exactly.
Brian：主要是整理现有机制，严格说不算新功能。

97
00:08:08,375 --> 00:08:18,002
Before this, declaring which dimensions of your input can vary at runtime meant a different mechanism depending on whether you were using torch.
以前，要声明输入的哪些维度能在运行时变化，得看你用的是 torch.compile、

98
00:08:18,002 --> 00:08:20,692
compile, torch. export, or make_fx.
torch.export 还是 make_fx：各有一套机制。

99
00:08:20,692 --> 00:08:24,114
Ava: So three different ways to say the same thing.
Ava：也就是同一件事有三种写法。

100
00:08:24,114 --> 00:08:28,786
Brian: Right, and the declaration usually lived far away from the model code.
Brian：对，而且这些声明通常离模型代码很远。

101
00:08:28,786 --> 00:08:37,880
Now you define a shape spec once, attach it to your function with a decorator, and all three entry points pick it up automatically.
现在只需定义一次形状规范，用装饰器挂到函数上，三个入口就会自动识别。

102
00:08:37,880 --> 00:08:42,982
Ava: And platform support — I saw ROCm and Rubin mentioned.
Ava：平台支持方面，我看到提到了 ROCm 和 Rubin。

103
00:08:42,982 --> 00:08:51,313
Brian: ROCm 7. 14 wheels now build from AMD's TheRock SDK. Intel XPU gets native graph capture.
Brian：ROCm 7.14 的 wheel 包现在由 AMD 的 TheRock SDK 构建。Intel XPU 也支持原生计算图捕获了。

104
00:08:51,313 --> 00:08:58,764
And Inductor now targets Rubin, NVIDIA's next architecture after Blackwell.
Inductor 现在也支持 NVIDIA 继 Blackwell 之后的新架构 Rubin。

105
00:08:58,764 --> 00:09:02,570
Ava: Anything we should flag as not fully baked yet?
Ava：有什么功能还不够成熟，需要提醒大家吗？

106
00:09:02,570 --> 00:09:08,367
Brian: Almost everything in this release is tagged API Unstable, so expect some churn.
Brian：这次发布的功能几乎都标为 API Unstable，后续可能会有调整。

107
00:09:08,367 --> 00:09:10,715
Complex-tensor support in torch.
torch.compile 对复数张量的支持

108
00:09:10,715 --> 00:09:16,585
compile is explicitly experimental — not every complex operation is covered yet.
仍明确处于实验阶段，尚未覆盖所有复数运算。

109
00:09:16,585 --> 00:09:22,601
And Python 3. 15 support landed, but it's eager-mode only for now — calling torch.
Python 3.15 已获支持，但目前仅限即时执行模式；调用 torch.compile

110
00:09:22,601 --> 00:09:28,528
compile under 3. 15 just raises an error rather than quietly running slower.
在 Python 3.15 下会直接报错，而不会悄悄地以较慢速度运行。

111
00:09:28,528 --> 00:09:34,974
Ava: Good to know before someone upgrades blind. So, wrapping up — three things to remember?
Ava：这得提醒准备升级的人。最后，有哪三点值得记住？

112
00:09:34,974 --> 00:09:42,380
Brian: One: NVGEMM brings epilogue fusion and low-precision support to PyTorch's fastest matmul path.
Brian：第一，NVGEMM 为 PyTorch 最快的矩阵乘法路径带来了尾声融合和低精度支持。

113
00:09:42,380 --> 00:09:50,573
Two: fault tolerance and one-sided memory access are now built into distributed training, not bolted on.
第二，容错和单边内存访问现已内置于分布式训练，而不是后加的功能。

114
00:09:50,573 --> 00:09:57,620
Three: Apple Silicon finally gets native linear algebra and a major decode-speed fix.
